#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:174
#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:243
msgid ""
"Example of Single Row: If the order is in row 5, enter \"5\" in both boxes "
"and click to sync."
msgstr ""

#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:175
#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:244
msgid ""
"Example of Multiple Rows: If orders are listed in rows 5-10, input \"5\" and "
"\"10\" in the respective boxes and initiate the sync."
msgstr ""

#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:183
msgid "Order Status Sync Configuration: Sheet to WooCommerce Update"
msgstr ""

#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:187
#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:255
msgid ""
"This configuration includes two selection boxes for specifying the range of "
"rows to sync.\n"
"              Example of Single Row: If you've added an order in row 5, "
"input '5' in both boxes and click to sync.\n"
"              Example of Multiple Rows: If orders are listed in rows 5 "
"through 10, input '5' and '10' in the respective boxes and click to sync."
msgstr ""

#: includes/pages/wc-product-sheet.php:194
msgid ""
"Order Id can not be empty in the sheet. If an Order Id is not present in the "
